    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d167">

                <pb facs="0229" n="161" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg161"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1469.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-10-26"><hi rendition="#italic">October
                                26,</hi> 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I Have to acknowledge the reception this
                    morning of despatch No. 2074, of the 15th instant, from the department, on the
                    cases of Colonel Nagle and Captain Warren.</p>
                <p>Although I have instructed Mr. West to transmit to you from Dublin the published
                    reports of the trial, I venture, for farther security, to send herewith a copy
                    of the Dublin Evening Mail, containing a report of the charge of the lord chief
                    baron to the jury at the opening</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d167-a1.xml" xpointer="d167-a1"/>
            </div>
